  "note": "OFM competition id -> EA league id for every competition logo built from EA's league-logo pack (leagues/l<id>.dds in leagues.zip). `leagues` is derived: each pair is a row of the pinned FC 27 leagues table and the competition the importer builds from it (leagueCompetitionId in lib/mapping.mjs); tools/eafc-import/badges-from-crest-pack.mjs --write-league-crosswalk regenerates it and CI diffs the result against this file. `authored` cannot be derived -- that table lists no cups, super cups or UEFA competitions -- so each entry was identified by looking at the artwork, and `name` records what it shows. `authored` also names the competitions the importer builds from EA's career-mode structure files (data/fc27-compdata): one that those files describe under an EA league id listed here, and whose clubs the package has, is authored under this competitionId and named `name` without the sponsor in parentheses. That is 27 of these ids today (22 domestic cups, five continental competitions); the others are reserved for the day the importer authors that competition, and are a naming convention rather than a checked fact. Committed so the logos can be rebuilt -- and reviewed -- without the EA database: scripts/build-club-badges.mjs consumes it.",
